Hi Zsófia,

In Zelig's new version, predicted and expected values are stored in another
address. There is no *sim.weak$qi$ev*. You should use
*sim.weak$qi[[1]]* or*sim.weak$ev1
* instead.
For more details, call *str(sim.weak$qi).*
*
*
*
*
Here it is your function. It is apparently working well:



##############################################
rm(list=ls())
library(Zelig)
library(ZeligChoice)

data(mexico)

dem.func<-function(aaa,bbb,ccc){
  z.out<-zelig(as.factor(vote88)~pristr + othcok + othsocok,
model="mlogit", data=mexico)
  options = list(z.out, pristr=aaa, othcok=bbb, othsocok=ccc)
  x.weak<-do.call(setx, options)
  sim.weak <- sim(z.out, x.weak)
  predicted <- data.frame(*sim.weak$qi[[1]]*) ###getting data.frame for
predicted probabilities
  return (predicted)

}

dem.func(1,2,3)
##############################################


best,

----
Rogério Jerônimo Barbosa
Sociology PhD Student at USP - São Paulo, Brazil
Researcher at Center for Metropolitan Studies (Cem/Cebrap)



